# Lines starting with a hash are notes for whoever edits the file: the song itself never shows them.
{title: Home on the Range}
{subtitle: My Western Home}
{artist: Traditional American}
{composer: Daniel E. Kelley}
{lyricist: Brewster M. Higley}
{year: 1872}
{key: G}
{capo: 2}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{duration: 3:20}
{tag: Demo}
{tag: Easy}
{tag: Singalong}
{meta: language en}

{comment_italic: Written as a poem in Kansas and set to music soon after, it was sung around cattle drive campfires long before anyone knew who wrote it.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh, [G]give me a [G7]home where the [C]buffalo [Cm]roam
Where the [G/B]deer and the [Em]antelope [A7]play [D7]
Where [G]seldom is [G7]heard a dis[C]couraging [Cm]word
And the [G]skies are not [D7]cloudy all [G]day
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[*Everybody] [D7]Home, [G]home on the [C]range
Where the [G/B]deer and the [Em]antelope [A7]play [D7]
Where [G]seldom is [G7]heard a dis[C]couraging [Cm]word
And the [G]skies are not [D7]cloudy all [G]day
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
How [G]often at [G7]night when the [C]heavens are [Cm]bright
With the [G/B]light from the [Em]glittering [A7]stars [D7]
Have I [G]stood here a[G7]mazed and [C]asked as I [Cm]gazed
If their [G]glory ex[D7]ceeds that of [G]ours
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Where the [G]air is so [G7]pure and the [C]zephyrs so [Cm]free
And the [G/B]breezes so [Em]balmy and [A7]light [D7]
That I [G]would not ex[G7]change my [C]home on the [Cm]range
For [G]all of the [D7]cities so [G]bright
{end_of_verse}

{chorus: Last chorus, slowing down}
